foreign  welcome to another installment of Harry  Potter Theory today we're going to be  discussing the magical School bobert  Hall if I asked you about bobotal  Academy of magic I better could guess  what you'd say it's one of the three  largest visiting schools in all of  Europe and it also happens to be one of  the snobbiest am I right after all who  could forget Fleur de la cause cruel  words during the Hogwarts Yule Ball even  though she was attending the event as a  guest she wasted no time comparing the  festivities to the ones her famous  French school held and Fleur wasn't kind  in her comparison from the decorations  to the presence of friendly ghosts Fleur  was hard-pressed to find anything she  liked but bobator was more than just a  school for the high and torti its  students are among the most accomplished  Wizards and witches in the entire  Wizarding World and when it came to  fighting against dark wizard and witches  Hogwarts alumni could find no better  allies than the graduates of bulbatore  especially when compared to durmstrang  the place where far darker Wizards and  witches seemed to graduate So today  we're going to take a step back and dive  into the depths of history as we take a  look at how bobotal came to be and why  it Rivals Hogwarts as one of the  greatest Wizarding schools in the world  early history it's hard to avoid  comparing bobaton to Hogwarts the two  seem to go hand in hand and even when we  look back at the very first day bovato  opened its doors we have to first  reference Hogwarts and that British  schools early history because bobaton's  established date is a bit of a mystery  we know that they were up and running by  the end of the 13th century that much is  sure they must have been since they were  one of the competitors in the Triumph  was a tournament which began around 12  19 A.D  but it'd be hard to say exactly how many  years before then they started Hogwarts  itself was founded around 990 so he  wouldn't be wrong to Guess that bombatol  also got their start by that point and  just like Hogwarts it only took a short  time for bombatol to become a  world-renowned school and the  destination for Europe's most affluent  Wizarding families unlike Hogwarts which  attracted students from the British  Isles bobotal recruited from all over  Continental Europe the location of its  Palace certainly helped add to its  appeal while Hogwarts was tucked away in  the cold Scottish Highlands the Palace  of bombatol was situated in the resort  town of Cairns in southern France right  across the sea from Corsica at least  that's what the earliest histories tell  us later different texts claim that the  palace was actually located in the  Pyrenees Mountains whatever the case may  have been the school grounds were  undoubtedly gorgeous they were covered  in Lush flower-filled Gardens and ornate  ancient statues even though Fleur could  have been a bit Kinder when bragging  about her school she certainly wasn't  wrong when it came to Beauty there were  few magical institutes that could  compare with bobatal  and even their mode of transportation  reflected that while most other Wizards  and witchers navigated the world aboard  their broomsticks and occasionally an  enchanted motorcycle the students at  bobato had a more elegant ride they  often used flying horses of course we  all saw that when Madame olymp Maxime  the headmistress of bomitor escorted her  students to the revived try was a  tournament in 1994. they rode carriages  drawn by abrax and horses and students  who are even rumored to ride them alone  even though it was against Wizarding  laws while Hogwarts allowed ghosts to  take up residence on its grounds The  Faculty at bombetor forbaded but there  were other magical creatures that called  the school home most famously bobato's  Great Hall was filled with wood nymphs  while the students ate their meals the  wood nymphs would serenade them with  Angelic songs which would be quite a  treat if you've only ever been used to  watching nearly headless  yank his head from his shoulders during  the holiday season the wood nymphs were  accompanied by Ice statues that sparkled  in the candlelight curriculum when it  comes to curriculum the Wizards and  witches of bobotal might have had an  advantage of their Hogwarts peers even  though both schools were comparable the  students at bomota started their testing  a full year after their fellow students  at Hogwarts that meant they were able to  focus on more Practical Magic instead of  focusing on Note memorization as the  boys and girls at Hogwarts School were  forced to do and just like Hogwarts  bobato didn't teach their students about  the dark arts while Europe's other great  magical School The durmstrang Institute  instructed their pupils in the basic  tenets of dark magic bobitor actively  avoided it but you don't really need to  pour over the class schedules of bobotal  to judge their curriculum if you take  one look at the French Academy's  performance in the tri-wizard tournament  then you can see just how skilled their  faculty and students were they had over  60 victories in the games and only  trailed behind Hogwarts by one  Championship famous graduates now if  you're not sure why you've never heard  of bobert Hall's famous graduates the  fact is you have some of the greatest  Sorcerers and Alchemists in the history  of the Wizarding World graduated from  bobotal rest assured there were far more  interesting alumni than Fleur De La  Calle although she was no slouch herself  for starters boboton was a school where  Nikola Flamel studied in his youth if  you can't quite remember who Flamel was  don't worry you might know him by his  most famous creation the Philosopher's  Stone Flamel learned the secrets of  alchemy and used his Newfound knowledge  to create a stone capable of providing  an unnaturally long life that's how the  wizard managed to live for over six  centuries it could also turn metal into  gold it wasn't until the second Rise of  old Voldemort that Flamel wisely decided  to destroy his Stone and accept his own  death after all Flamel agreed with Albus  Dumbledore if the Philosopher's Stone  ever fell into Voldemort's hands the  world itself might have been destroyed  another famous wizard Vincent Duke  Detroit  in the 18th century during the  tumultuous French Revolution the wizard  cunningly used his magic a concealment  charm in particular to avoid a mob  execution and was one of a handful of  lucky ones to do that but among  bobaton's long list of graduates you  might recognize the oversized limp  Maxime she was the headmistress of the  academy during the Triumph was a  tournament of 1994. just like everyone  else she attended the games and  witnessed the first signs of Lord  Voldemort's return unlike Igor kakarov  the Headmaster of the durmstrang  institute's maxim wasn't fond of the  dark arts she quickly realized that  Albus Dumbledore would need her help to  fight against Voldemort and joined his  side when the Hogwarts Headmaster tried  to enlist Giants to his cause since  Maxim herself was rumored to be half  giant Dumbledore supposed that Maxim's  charms combined with Hagrid's Heritage  might be enough to sway the Giants the  small differences if we dive into the  nitty-gritty we can find a few more fun  differences between bobator and Hogwarts  as you might have expected this French  school's dress code was Far different  and even though the film suggested that  bobato only accepted female students  they allowed men to enroll as well when  running around their own Palace grounds  the students at bobator were expected to  wear their school's colors they often  wore short capes around their shoulders  during formal occasions but while  attending Class A simple skirt and  jacket for girls was acceptable and  presumably trousers and a jacket for  boys would have been as well and bobato  might have actually benefited from  having a long-lived Alchemist as one of  their graduates according to rumors the  school received a large annual gift from  the Flamel family wealth which he  amassed through the centuries in his  honor the school constructed a giant  water fountain in the center of its  largest Garden but it wasn't simply a  lovely water display there were tales  that this Fountain held mystical  properties that only an alchemist could  concoct Legacy when we look back at  bobato's long history and wonder what  type of Legacy they've etched out for  themselves it's hard to really pin it  down what we know of the school comes in  bits and pieces from sources in the  British Wizarding World those sources  famously favored Hogwarts and during the  life of Harry Potter most news coverage  centered around the second Rise of Lord  Voldemort who was a uniquely British  threat since the dark lord had not yet  launched an attack against Continental  Europe there was no reason for the  Wizards and witches of bombota to do  more than an offer Aid which they did  but that wasn't the type of thing that  made it into newspapers at least not  when Harry Potter was actively engaging  Death Eaters in combat but that's not  exactly their fault bobato is a great  school and one of the best in Europe it  never produced Heroes like Hogwarts but  it never produced dark Lords either in  the end it was a school and by the looks  of it a pretty good one and that's it  for this video do you have anything to  add about bobotal leave a comment down  below as always if you enjoyed the  content please like the video and  subscribe to the channel until next time  remember happiness can be found even in  the darkest of times if one only  remembers to turn on the light  foreign

